      "description": "**Question.** The paper's trial: can the monkey report the direction of weak motion placed in a neuron's receptive field?\n\n**On screen.** Panel 1: [[param:stimulus_duration]] of random dots in an aperture over an example receptive field, fixation point on. Panel 2: dots and fixation point off, two targets on the motion axis.\n\n**The subject.** Holds gaze in the fixation window during the dots (enforced), then saccades to the target on the side of the motion. Juice if correct, a time-out if wrong.\n\n**Measured.** Choice at each correlation; correction trials after three errors in one direction are excluded.\n\n**Limits.** Aperture, axis and speed are examples, not matched to a neuron. The MT recording the paper compared against is not part of this folder.",
